<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept department store sales up 2.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept department store sales up 2.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at department stores in Japan in September were up 2.3 percent from a year earlier to 625.76 billion yen, marking the second consecutive month of year-on-year rises, the Japan Department Stores' Association said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The September survey covered 259 outlets of 108 companies, the association said in a statement.</p>
<p>Overall sales were up in September due to robust sales to individual shoppers, the association said, though it said sales to corporate customers stayed weak.</p>
<p>Demand for seasonal items was active, it said.</p>
</text>
